credible|believable|ADJECTIVE|believable|Supported well enough to deserve belief or trust.|đáng tin; có cơ sở để tin|Her account of the missing parcel sounded credible.|Lời kể của cô ấy về bưu kiện bị mất nghe có vẻ đáng tin.|Use credible with an account, explanation or source; it concerns whether something deserves belief.|credible
fill|make-full|VERB|make full|Put material into a container or space until little or no room remains.|làm đầy; đổ đầy|We filled the large jug with cold water.|Chúng tôi đổ đầy nước lạnh vào chiếc bình lớn.|Transitive: fill something with a substance; the container is the direct object.|fill
fill|enter-information|VERB|enter information|Write the details requested in a blank space or document.|điền thông tin|Please fill in your address on the first line.|Vui lòng điền địa chỉ của bạn vào dòng đầu tiên.|Use fill in for a detail or form; the particle is part of the construction shown here.|fill
position|location|NOUN|location or arrangement|The place where something is situated or the way it is arranged.|vị trí; tư thế|Check the position of the camera before recording.|Kiểm tra vị trí của máy quay trước khi ghi hình.|Countable; position of something identifies its location or arrangement.|position
position|place|VERB|put in place|Place an object in a particular spot or arrangement.|đặt vào vị trí|They positioned the lamp beside the reading chair.|Họ đặt đèn bên cạnh chiếc ghế đọc sách.|Transitive; a location phrase can follow the object.|position
position|job|NOUN|job or role|A job that someone holds or can apply for in an organization.|vị trí công việc; chức vụ|There is a vacant position in the accounts team.|Có một vị trí công việc còn trống trong nhóm kế toán.|Countable; a position in a team or organization refers to employment.|position
position|viewpoint|NOUN|viewpoint|An opinion or stance that someone takes on an issue.|quan điểm; lập trường|The committee has not stated its position on the proposal.|Ủy ban chưa nêu lập trường về đề xuất đó.|Use position on an issue; this sense concerns a view rather than a physical place.|position
dessert|sweet-course|NOUN|sweet final course|Sweet food eaten as the final part of a meal.|món tráng miệng ngọt|We shared a slice of pear tart for dessert.|Chúng tôi chia nhau một miếng bánh tart lê để tráng miệng.|Countable for a dish, or uncountable when naming the course; for dessert is a common pattern.|dessert
sophomore|second-year-student|NOUN|second-year college student|A student in the second year of study at a college or university in the US.|sinh viên năm thứ hai ở Hoa Kỳ|As a sophomore, Lina joined the university debate club.|Là sinh viên năm thứ hai, Lina tham gia câu lạc bộ tranh luận của trường đại học.|Countable; this draft covers the source-supported US college sense.|sophomore
tune|melody|NOUN|melody|A recognizable sequence of musical notes.|giai điệu|He hummed a cheerful tune while washing the dishes.|Anh ấy ngân nga một giai điệu vui tươi trong lúc rửa bát.|Countable; sing, hum or whistle a tune; only the noun is covered here.|tune
so|degree|ADVERB|great degree|To a degree emphasized by the speaker, sometimes with a stated result.|rất; đến mức|The corridor was so narrow that we walked in single file.|Hành lang hẹp đến mức chúng tôi đi thành một hàng.|Use so before an adjective or adverb; a that-clause can state the result.|so
so|statement-substitute|ADVERB|reference to a statement|Used in place of repeating an idea just mentioned, treating it as true.|như vậy; thế|Will the train arrive soon? I hope so.|Tàu sẽ đến sớm chứ? Tôi hy vọng là vậy.|In hope so or think so, so refers back to the preceding statement.|so
so|result|CONJUNCTION|introduce a result|Used to connect a situation with its consequence.|vì vậy; nên|The shop was closed, so we returned the next morning.|Cửa hàng đã đóng cửa nên chúng tôi quay lại vào sáng hôm sau.|Place the cause before so and the consequence after it; this construction does not express purpose.|so
consume|use-up|VERB|use a resource|Use a supply of energy, material or another resource.|tiêu thụ; sử dụng|The old heater consumes a lot of electricity.|Máy sưởi cũ tiêu thụ nhiều điện.|Transitive; consume energy or resources describes their use.|consume
consume|eat-drink|VERB|eat or drink|Take food or drink into the body.|ăn; uống; tiêu thụ thức ăn hoặc đồ uống|The guests consumed most of the fruit during the break.|Khách ăn gần hết số trái cây trong giờ nghỉ.|Transitive; relatively formal when referring to food or drink.|consume
let|allow|VERB|allow|Allow someone to act or allow a situation to occur.|cho phép; để cho|The guide let us take photographs in the courtyard.|Hướng dẫn viên cho phép chúng tôi chụp ảnh trong sân.|Use let plus object plus bare infinitive: let us take, without to.|let
require|need|VERB|need|Need something in order to work, happen or achieve a purpose.|cần; đòi hỏi|This repair requires a special tool.|Việc sửa chữa này cần một dụng cụ chuyên biệt.|Transitive in the source-supported need sense; the needed item is the object.|require
relief|reassurance|NOUN|release from worry|The feeling that comes when a worry or difficulty has ended or become less serious.|sự nhẹ nhõm|She felt relief when the missing tickets were found.|Cô ấy cảm thấy nhẹ nhõm khi những chiếc vé bị mất được tìm thấy.|Usually uncountable for the feeling; a sense of relief is a common construction.|relief
relief|pain-easing|NOUN|easing of pain|A reduction in pain or physical discomfort.|sự giảm đau; sự dịu bớt khó chịu|The cool cloth brought some relief from the discomfort.|Chiếc khăn mát giúp giảm bớt phần nào cảm giác khó chịu.|Uncountable; relief from pain or discomfort identifies what is eased.|relief
relief|emergency-aid|NOUN|aid in hardship|Practical help or supplies given to people facing disaster or severe hardship.|sự cứu trợ; hàng cứu trợ|Volunteers delivered relief supplies to the flooded villages.|Tình nguyện viên chuyển hàng cứu trợ đến những ngôi làng bị ngập lụt.|Usually uncountable; relief supplies and disaster relief refer to aid.|relief
dig|make-hole|VERB|remove earth|Move soil out of the ground to create a hole or open a space.|đào|The workers dug a narrow trench beside the fence.|Công nhân đào một rãnh hẹp cạnh hàng rào.|Past tense and past participle dug; dig a hole or trench is transitive.|dig
realm|field|NOUN|field of activity|An area of knowledge, thought or activity.|lĩnh vực; phạm vi|That question falls within the realm of public policy.|Câu hỏi đó nằm trong lĩnh vực chính sách công.|Use the realm of something or within a realm for an abstract field.|realm
realm|kingdom|NOUN|kingdom|A country or territory governed by a king or queen.|vương quốc|The queen travelled to the northern edge of her realm.|Nữ hoàng đi đến rìa phía bắc vương quốc của mình.|Countable; this is the monarch's territory sense.|realm
criterion|standard|NOUN|standard for judging|A standard used to evaluate something or make a choice.|tiêu chí|Durability was our main criterion for choosing the table.|Độ bền là tiêu chí chính của chúng tôi khi chọn chiếc bàn.|Singular criterion; plural criteria; criterion for a choice identifies its basis.|criterion
rural|countryside|ADJECTIVE|of the countryside|Connected with places in the countryside rather than towns or cities.|thuộc nông thôn|The charity supports libraries in rural communities.|Tổ chức từ thiện hỗ trợ các thư viện trong những cộng đồng nông thôn.|Use before a noun such as area or community; it does not imply poverty by itself.|rural
longing|strong-desire|NOUN|strong desire|A strong feeling of wanting something, often something absent or out of reach.|niềm khao khát; nỗi mong mỏi|After months abroad, he felt a longing for home.|Sau nhiều tháng ở nước ngoài, anh ấy cảm thấy nhớ mong quê nhà.|Use longing for something or longing to do something; this entry covers the noun.|longing
curb|restrain|VERB|restrain or limit|Limit an undesirable activity or prevent it from increasing.|kiềm chế; hạn chế|The new measures aim to curb unnecessary spending.|Các biện pháp mới nhằm hạn chế chi tiêu không cần thiết.|Transitive; curb an activity or increase does not necessarily mean ending it completely.|curb
awkward|embarrassing|ADJECTIVE|socially uncomfortable|Causing embarrassment or making a social situation uncomfortable.|khó xử; ngượng ngùng|Nobody replied, and the meeting fell into an awkward silence.|Không ai trả lời, và cuộc họp rơi vào sự im lặng đầy ngượng ngùng.|Use with a situation or moment that causes social discomfort.|awkward
awkward|hard-to-manage|ADJECTIVE|difficult to handle|Difficult or inconvenient to move, use or deal with.|khó thao tác; bất tiện|The wide cabinet was awkward to carry through the doorway.|Chiếc tủ rộng khó khiêng qua cửa.|Use awkward to do something when handling an object is inconvenient.|awkward
awkward|clumsy|ADJECTIVE|clumsy in movement|Moving without easy control or coordination.|vụng về; lóng ngóng|His awkward movements made the simple dance look difficult.|Những động tác vụng về của anh ấy khiến điệu nhảy đơn giản trông có vẻ khó.|Use with movement or someone moving clumsily; keep distinct from an inconvenient object.|awkward
promote|advertise|VERB|publicize|Draw attention to a product or service to increase interest in it.|quảng bá; quảng cáo|The shop uses short videos to promote its new products.|Cửa hàng dùng những video ngắn để quảng bá các sản phẩm mới.|Transitive; promote a product or service in the publicity sense.|promote
promote|encourage|VERB|encourage development|Support an activity or help it become more common or successful.|khuyến khích; thúc đẩy|The school runs events to promote healthy eating.|Trường tổ chức các sự kiện để khuyến khích ăn uống lành mạnh.|Transitive; promote an activity or development need not involve commercial advertising.|promote
promote|raise-rank|VERB|give a higher rank|Move someone to a higher job or rank.|thăng chức; thăng cấp|The company promoted Sara to team leader.|Công ty thăng chức cho Sara lên trưởng nhóm.|Use promote someone to a position; the employee is the object.|promote
bent|not-straight|ADJECTIVE|not straight|Curved or angled away from a straight shape.|bị cong; không thẳng|The bent metal rod would not fit into the frame.|Thanh kim loại bị cong không vừa với khung.|Use bent for an object that is no longer straight; only this source-supported adjective sense is covered.|bent
